# Siya visuals — slide-by-slide approval gate

When the user asks for a **carousel or static image** (Siya Health brand creative), do **not** produce the full pack in one pass.

## Phase 1 — copy plan only

1. Draft on-frame copy deck in chat or `copy/carousel.md`
2. No captions, video prompts, tracker rows, or WorkDrive yet
3. Stop and wait for approval before any render

## Phase 2 — one image at a time

1. Render **slide 1 only** (source photo + `compose_*.py`)
2. Show it in chat; self-audit: Style Lock tokens · soft dissolve · lean A-03 · face-safe · right-weighted
3. Wait for approval before slide 2+
4. If the user locks style (“rest look good, continue”), later slides may batch

## Phase 3 — only after the user says “approved”

When (and only when) the user explicitly approves:

1. Remaining slides if needed
2. Captions · video-prompt · tracker row · `SHIP.md` (phase 3 + approved) — under `editorial-packs/[ID]/` or `statics/[ID]/`
3. Agents **do not** call Zoho APIs or hold refresh tokens. After the pack lands on **`main`**, GitHub Action **Siya WorkDrive Phase-3 sync (live)** mirrors changed packs into WorkDrive `_API-DRY-RUN/04–07` (fresh delivery folders; existing secrets)
4. End by stating: **Pack ready in git** + folder path, and that WorkDrive sync will run from Actions into `_API-DRY-RUN/`

## Precedence (WorkDrive)

- No WorkDrive before Phase 3 approval in chat
- Agents never auto-sync via TrueSync/API themselves
- Human gate = chat approval → `SHIP.md` + tracker on `main` → Action syncs

## Never skip

- Do not invent layouts — classify → template ID → compose
- Do not treat `GenerateImage` output as the final branded frame
- Automated ship gates do **not** replace founder/lead visual OK
- Lean A-03 default: headline + one `--recognition` line only (no on-frame explanation/takeaway unless `--dense`)
